# REST Action Validation

## Always wrap with `Validate()`

Every REST endpoint in `setup-*-rest-api.ts` must be wrapped with `Validate({ schema, schemaName })` to enforce schema validation on URL params, query, and body. The `furystack/rest-action-validate-wrapper` lint rule enforces this.

```typescript
// ✅ Validate wraps the action
'/files/:letter/:path/stream': Authenticate()(
  Validate({ schema: mediaApiSchema, schemaName: 'StreamFileEndpoint' })(StreamAction),
),

// ❌ raw input reaches the action
'/files/:letter/:path/master.m3u8': Authenticate()(HlsMasterAction),
```

Built-in framework actions (`GetCurrentUser`, `LogoutAction`, etc.) handle validation internally — wrap them with `Validate()` only when the framework signature requires it; otherwise add a justified `eslint-disable` comment.

## Validate user-controlled params before system calls

Even with `Validate()`, action handlers passing user input to system processes (FFmpeg, file system, shell) **must** explicitly validate critical parameters. Schema validation alone doesn't guarantee bounds, mode whitelist, or numeric range.

```typescript
// ✅ explicit bounds checking before FFmpeg
const segmentIndex = parseInt(index, 10)
if (isNaN(segmentIndex) || segmentIndex < 0) {
  throw new RequestError('Invalid segment index', 400)
}
if (from < 0 || to <= from) {
  throw new RequestError('Invalid time range', 400)
}

const VALID_MODES: PlaybackMode[] = ['direct-play', 'remux', 'direct-stream', 'transcode']
if (!VALID_MODES.includes(mode)) {
  throw new RequestError('Invalid playback mode', 400)
}

// ❌ unvalidated parseInt / negative values reach FFmpeg
const segmentIndex = parseInt(index, 10)
ffmpegArgs.push('-ss', String(from))
```

## Path traversal prevention

When constructing file paths from user input, always validate against directory traversal. The router does **not** filter `..` or null bytes.

```typescript
// ✅ explicit traversal check
if (path.includes('..') || path.includes('\0')) {
  throw new RequestError('Invalid path', 400)
}

// ✅ resolve + relative containment check
const resolvedPath = resolve(baseDir, userInputPath)
const rel = relative(baseDir, resolvedPath)
if (rel.startsWith('..') || isAbsolute(rel)) {
  throw new RequestError('Invalid path', 400)
}
```
